From d9770ef69eaeebe643ba83caeac8934ef33acef2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code Review <claude-review@example.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 06:41:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add password reset flow and Terms/Privacy pages
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Password reset:
- prisma: add resetTokenHash (unique) and resetTokenExpires to User,
  with a matching migration
- src/lib/passwordReset.js: generate a random token, store only its
  SHA-256 hash (same principle as passwords — a leaked DB can't be
  used to reset accounts)
- src/lib/email.js: thin Resend wrapper; falls back to console
  logging when RESEND_API_KEY isn't set, so local dev works without
  email configured
- api/auth/forgot-password: rate-limited by IP, always returns the
  same generic response whether or not the account exists (no
  account-enumeration via this endpoint), 1-hour token expiry
- api/auth/reset-password: validates token + expiry, sets the new
  password, clears the token so it can't be reused
- forgot-password.js / reset-password.js: matching pages
- index.js: add a "Forgot password?" link in login mode

Terms/Privacy:
- add /terms and /privacy as static pages, linked from the register
  form; both are explicitly labeled as a generic starting template,
  not legal advice, since actual legal review matters once this has
  real users beyond the two of you

- .env.example: document RESEND_API_KEY / EMAIL_FROM
- package.json: add resend dependency, regenerate lockfile
